# ASI Prototype -- Adaptive Symbolic Interface

## What This Project Is
A patient-facing web app prototype for pain management through personalized
symbolic interventions ("placebo boosters"). Designed for clinical trial use
under clinician supervision. Target demo audience: pain clinic doctors/researchers.

## Tech Stack
- Frontend: React 18+ with TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind CSS, built as a PWA
- Backend: Python 3.11+ with FastAPI
- Database: PostgreSQL with SQLAlchemy + Alembic migrations
- AI: OpenAI GPT-4o for session script generation
- Audio: OpenAI TTS API for text-to-speech
- Auth: JWT-based (patient vs clinician roles)
- Environment: Windows native (no WSL/Docker)

## Project Structure
- frontend/ -- React PWA app
- backend/ -- FastAPI application
- Full build plan: .cursor/plans/asi_prototype_plan.md

## Code Style
- TypeScript with strict mode for frontend
- Python type hints for backend
- Pydantic schemas for API validation
- UI should be clinical, trustworthy, calming (blues/whites/grays)
- Mobile-first responsive design